@startuml PropORACLE_Ticket_Design
' Ticket design — dual card build, construction rules, publish
' Scheduled re-publishers (payout capture, keep scrub) are separate flows below.
' Render: PlantUML extension or https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title PropORACLE — Ticket design (Goblin-70 + mixer)

|Build (per run_daily / refresh / late_fetch)|
start
:Sport step8 workbooks\n(step8_*_direction_clean.xlsx);

:combined_slate_tickets.py --write-web;
note right
  Graded-main mixer / grade pool.
  Eligibility = mixer ""filter_eligible""
  (pipeline_read_checklist.json) —
  **not** the G70 gate stack.
  Does not own live /tickets alone.
end note

:Construction rules (mixer);
note right
  1. MLB construction ban runs **first**
     for every MAIN slip (ce04cad8c),
     before core_build / strong_builder.
  2. Same-player multistat hard block
     (utils/ticket_diversity.py).
  3. Diversity filter
     (config/diversity_config.json).
  (Anchor cap is **not** here —
   it runs after dual-card merge.)
end note

if (Caller routes through\nInvoke-G70WriteWebStandalone?) then (yes)
  :build_goblin70_tickets.py --write-web\n(via Invoke-G70WriteWebStandalone);
  note right
    Day-ahead / 1AM / 5AM / MLB fill /
    late_fetch / refresh / Publish-LiveSite
    (Tee-Object fallback if
    Invoke-LoggedPwsh.ps1 missing).
  end note
else (no — known gap)
  :build_goblin70_tickets.py --write-web\n(direct py in run_daily.ps1 STEP D-G70);
  note right
    **Gap:** run_daily.ps1 still calls py
    directly, not the standalone helper.
    Logging / ordering only —
    exposure trim still runs inside
    the dual-card write (both paths).
  end note
endif

:Assemble dual card;
note right
  Goblin-70 groups **first**.
  Patch mixer **lines** from this fetch.
  Merge **full** graded-main pool under.
  Keep mixer groups that left the live board.
end note

fork
  :Goblin Power 3\n(all-Goblin);
fork again
  :Flex 4\n(all-Standard or 1 Std +\nGoblin leftovers);
fork again
  :YOLO Power 4/5/6\n(Diamond/Platinum seeds;\n**excluded from ticket WR / Income**);
end fork

:Cross-ticket anchor cap\n(trim_payload_slate_exposure);
note right
  Runs on the **merged** dual card,
  before tickets_latest.json
  (so 9PM payout capture prices
  the trimmed card).
  include_goblin70=True — one ledger
  walks **G70 first**, then
  CORE / STRONG / mixer.
  G70 wins ties; CORE/mixer lose them.
  Caps: anchor ≤1 + non-anchor ≤1;
  blocks identical player+prop+dir
  (McGreevy / Wood ×8 class).
  Worst case: same player twice
  (once as anchor, once not) —
  same leg cannot appear twice.
end note

:tickets_latest.json\n(disk: ui_runner/runtime/\nGitHub: ui_runner/templates/);
:Publish-LiveSite.ps1 → origin/main;
:Railway GET /tickets\nrenders prebuilt JSON\n(no rebuild at request time);
stop

|Scheduled re-publishers|
start
:Task Scheduler window;
split
  :run_live_payout_capture.ps1;
  note right
    See payout-scrape.puml.
    Holds payout_capture.lock,
    writes N-correct floors,
    then **publishes on its own**.
  end note
split again
  :scrub_goblin70_keep_live.py\n(run_g70_keep_scrub.ps1);
  note right
    Default: --write --publish-live
    (opt out with -SkipPublish).
    On keep fail: **drops the whole
    G70 ticket** (not a shrunk Power 2
    / 1-leg). Off-board legs untouched.
    Writes runtime + templates (+ main_cp),
    then Publish-LiveSite on drops.
    Does **not** clear live_cdp
    (survivors keep floors; dropped
    slips are gone).
    Capture write-back is a **merge by
    ticket_id** (not a card snapshot),
    so a lost race no longer resurrects
    dropped / rebuilt-away slips.
    Shared tickets_write.lock still TODO.
    Reverse race (scrub after capture
    clears fresh floors) is harmless —
    next window re-scrapes missing live_cdp.
  end note
end split
:Publish-LiveSite.ps1 → origin/main;
note right
  Capture publishes itself (confirmed).
  Scrub also publishes on drops by
  default (confirmed).
end note
stop

legend bottom
  **Gates — keep files can REPLACE the generic stack, not only add**
  Baseline 70% engine: directional L5=5 + L10>=8 + D + cover.
  Keep-file overrides (examples):
    · MLB pitcher Goblins → L10-primary (not the L5=5 stack)
    · MLB Standard → hard-banned on G70
    · CFB Pass Yards Goblin OVER → D skipped
    · Tennis / Soccer / CFB / WNBA / NFL → sport keep modules
  Payout figure = N-correct (Flex / Power), never 1st place.
  Checkout gate changes are **not live** until main_cp rebuild + Publish-LiveSite.
endlegend

@enduml
